<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
com.throne.throne-backend.plist — throne-owned macOS LaunchAgent template for
the throne-backend NestJS cron host (keep-going, no-idling, dispatch, the
status writer and every other hosted worker); the mac counterpart of
throne/systemd/throne-backend.service.

Not loadable as it stands: `{{THRONE_ROOT}}` (absolute path of the throne
directory) and `{{NODE_BIN}}` (absolute path of the node interpreter, resolved
through mise's `lts` symlink) are substituted at install time, and only the
rendered copy in the user's LaunchAgents dir is a working agent. Install with:
  cd <throne root> && ./install.sh        (or ./bin/throne-cli install-services)

Enabled and bootstrapped by install-services, exactly like its systemd twin.
The pre-consolidation com.throne.keep-going and com.throne.no-idling agents
this process replaces are retired (RETIRED_DARWIN_AGENTS in
src/install-services/darwin.ts) and booted out before this one is bootstrapped,
so no second dispatch loop ever delivers into live panes twice.

THE WATCH LOOP IS THE SERVICE, same as on linux (systemd/throne-backend.service,
2026-08-26): the long-lived process is the Nest CLI in --watch mode and the
app is its CHILD. A bad build crash-loops in the child; launchd never sees an
exit, and fixing the source recompiles and relaunches automatically.

KEYS SHIPPED BELOW
  Label             a launchctl service target is built from this label
                    rather than from the filename.
  ProgramArguments  /bin/bash as a login shell wrapping the exact argv the
                    linux ExecStart uses. The login shell is not optional
                    here: `nest start --watch` spawns its child as the bare
                    word `node` through a shell, and the hosted workers spawn
                    git, gh, herdr and the harness launchers by name — all of
                    which live on the PATH the .profile chain builds, not on
                    launchd's bare system PATH. --path is RELATIVE on purpose
                    (nest-cli rejects an absolute tsconfig path; see the
                    linux unit), which WorkingDirectory below makes safe.
                    Output goes to ~/Library/Logs/throne/ for want of a
                    journal; StandardOutPath does not expand ~, hence the
                    redirect inside the shell.
  WorkingDirectory  the rendered throne root. launchd.plist(5): "This optional
                    key is used to specify a directory to chdir(2) to before
                    running the job."
  RunAtLoad         launchd.plist(5): "This optional key is used to control
                    whether your job is launched once at the time the job is
                    loaded. The default is false."
  KeepAlive         launchd.plist(5): "The value may be set to true to
                    unconditionally keep the job alive." Stands in for the
                    linux unit's Restart=always.
  ThrottleInterval  launchd.plist(5): "by default, jobs will not be spawned
                    more than once every 10 seconds." 10 is that documented
                    default; the linux unit's RestartSec=3 is not reproduced.

NOT REPRODUCED from the linux unit, deliberately: `Type=notify`,
`WatchdogSec=` and the READY=1 handshake are systemd-only. sd_notify is a
documented no-op when NOTIFY_SOCKET is unset (src/throne-backend/sd-notify.ts),
so the same code runs here without a watchdog; a hung-but-alive backend on a
mac is restarted by an operator, not by launchd.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>com.throne.throne-backend</string>
	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>/bin/bash</string>
		<string>-lc</string>
		<string>mkdir -p "$HOME/Library/Logs/throne" &amp;&amp; exec {{NODE_BIN}} {{THRONE_ROOT}}/node_modules/@nestjs/cli/bin/nest.js start --watch --path tsconfig.build.json &gt;&gt; "$HOME/Library/Logs/throne/throne-backend.log" 2&gt;&amp;1</string>
	</array>
	<key>WorkingDirectory</key>
	<string>{{THRONE_ROOT}}</string>
	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<true/>
	<key>KeepAlive</key>
	<true/>
	<key>ThrottleInterval</key>
	<integer>10</integer>
</dict>
</plist>
